    <task id="task_contrato-empresarial_Servir_um_pedido_de_infer_ncia" name="Servir um pedido de inferência">
      <documentation>notation position: none stated, and the filing says why: none. `none` means somebody looked and this operation is in no process notation, `unmeasured` means a notation exists and nobody has found this operation in it, `notApplicable` means this filing has no notation to point into. An absent position is not a gap in the filing: the filing says which of the three it is. [assets/sqlc/entries/operations.sqlc]</documentation>
    </task>
    <textAnnotation id="note_contrato-empresarial_cover">
      <text>A dashed box is a group, not a container: it gathers the operations that induce demand into one layer, and an operation may be in several. [assets/sqlc/diagrams/categories.sqlc]</text>
    </textAnnotation>
    <textAnnotation id="note_contrato-empresarial_lane">
      <text>An empty lane is a layer nothing draws on, not an idle one: every layer carries figures, and BPMN has no glyph to show them. [assets/sqlc/diagrams/lane_grain.sqlc]</text>
    </textAnnotation>
    <textAnnotation id="note_contrato-empresarial_scope">
      <text>Scope: unbounded. The pool is the whole system only when the filing says `complete`. [assets/sqlc/diagrams/scopes.sqlc]</text>
    </textAnnotation>
    <textAnnotation id="note_contrato-empresarial_search">
      <text>Coupling search: unmeasured. An absent dependence line is not independence. [assets/sqlc/diagrams/searches.sqlc]</text>
    </textAnnotation>
